---
title: Easy Chicken Curry
description: A comforting one-pan chicken curry with tender chicken simmered in a spiced tomato and coconut sauce, finished with baby spinach.
course: main
cuisine: Indian-Inspired
servings: 4
time required: 45 minutes
prep time: 15 minutes
cook time: 30 minutes
source: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MmU1sXsnp3s
image: https://downshiftology.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/Coconut-Curry-Chicken-main-500x500.jpg
tags: [chicken, curry, coconut, weeknight, one-pan]
---

Heat @vegetable oil{2%tbsp} in a #large pan{} over medium-high heat. Add @chicken breasts{3}(approx 500g, chopped into bite-size chunks) and cook for ~{5-6%minutes} until browned all over. Remove the chicken to a plate and set aside.

Lower the heat to medium and add @onion{1%large}(peeled and finely chopped). Cook for ~{5%minutes} until softened, then stir in @garlic{2%cloves}(minced) and @minced ginger{2%tsp} and cook for ~{1%minute} until fragrant.

Stir in @mild curry powder{2%tbsp}, @ground coriander{1%tbsp}, @ground cumin{1/2%tbsp}, @paprika{1%tsp}, @ground cinnamon{1/2%tsp}, @salt{1/2%tsp}, and @black pepper{1/2%tsp}. Cook for ~{1%minute} to toast the spices.

Add @tomato paste{2%tbsp} and stir to combine, then pour in @finely chopped tomatoes{400%g}(1 tin), @chicken stock{240%ml}, and @full fat coconut milk{400%ml}(1 tin). Stir well.

Return the chicken to the pan, bring to a simmer, and cook for ~{15%minutes}, stirring occasionally, until the chicken is cooked through and the sauce has thickened.

For a thicker sauce, stir in @cornflour{1%tbsp}(mixed with 2 tbsp cold water to make a slurry) and simmer for another ~{2%minutes}.

Stir in @baby spinach{60%g}(2 packed cups) and cook until just wilted, ~{1-2%minutes}.

Serve over @boiled rice{} and garnish with @fresh coriander{} and @chilli flakes{}.
